  "claimBoundary": "Panels A and the reference curves are analytic formulas. Producer and independent markers are deterministic finite bilateral-lattice calculations. The Bessel theorem is proved on the infinite bilateral lattice, while finite calculations only corroborate it. G is the normalized row mass in rescaled time at selected positive target roots. The family has one carrier, does not establish a normalized nonlinear Navier-Stokes lower bound, is not DNS, and proves no regularity or blow-up statement.",
